(* q-secrecy.pvl
   The secrecy query of the session models about what the server sends (AUD-5, #389; AUD-6, #409). None is conditional
   on a leak: a model has the compromise of its scenario or it has none, and expected.tsv says which of them hold there.
   The password is in q-password.pvl, since only the session with a Login has one. *)

(* What the server sends in a session of alice: a record of the data stream, or on the control stream the Update *)
(* @query sec-data *)
query sid: sessionid; attacker(appdata(bob, alice, sid)).
